<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mori Motonari</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1497">1497</a>–<a href="/years/1571">1571</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mori Motonari was a Japanese warlord of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sengoku-period">Sengoku period</a> from Aki province. Starting as a minor lord, he defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sue-harukata">Sue Harukata</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-miyajima">Battle of Itsukushima</a> in 1555, absorbed the lands of the Ouchi and then destroyed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amago-clan">Amago clan</a> in 1566. By his death the Mori controlled most of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chugoku-region">Chugoku</a> region of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/honshu">Honshu</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mori-motonari.jpg" alt="Mori Motonari" width="320" height="661" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mori_Motonari.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
